  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.271,
            0.106
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, ∠1 = ∠2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.106,
            0.679,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, by the AAS congruence condition, ∆BAD ≅ ∆DCB."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.124,
            0.847,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, AD = CB, and DC = BA, since these are corresponding sides of congruent triangles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.164,
            0.548,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is it wrong to write ∆BAD ≅ ∆CDB? Why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.189,
            0.848,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, we have established that if all the angles of a quadrilateral are right angles, then the opposite sides have equal lengths. Therefore, the quadrilateral is a rectangle. Thus, a rectangle can simply be defined as follows —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.268,
            0.846,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Rectangle:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A rectangle is a quadrilateral in which the angles are all 90°. Let us list the properties of a rectangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.316,
            0.621,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Property 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " All the angles of a rectangle are 90°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.341,
            0.691,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Property 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The opposite sides of a rectangle are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.371,
            0.606,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Are the opposite sides of a rectangle parallel?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.396,
            0.847,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "They definitely seem so. This fact can be justified using one of the transversal properties."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.434,
            0.558,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Notice that AB acts as a transversal to AD and BC, and that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathbf{A} + \\angle \\mathbf{B} = 90^{\\circ} + 90^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.47,
            0.56,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the sum of the internal angles on the same side of the transversal is 180°, the lines are parallel. We can use this fact to conclude that the lines AD and BC are parallel, which we represent as AD || BC."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.562,
            0.559,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you similarly show that AB is parallel to DC (AB||DC)?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.564,
            0.434,
            0.893,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.564,
                0.434,
                0.893,
                0.588
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.604,
            0.844,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Property 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The opposite sides of a rectangle are parallel to each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.628,
            0.847,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Property 4:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The diagonals of a rectangle are of equal length and they bisect each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.674,
            0.394,
            0.696
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Special Rectangle"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
